    {
      "type": "Text",
      "props": {
        "id": "Text-e0c3ae18-3e88-4748-ac63-0fcbab6755f2",
        "text": "<p>The handloom scarf is made by attaching two panels on the two opposite short sides to increase the length of a waste fabric piece to make a scarf out of it. The attachment is done by doing white embroidery on the two joints. A hand made, beaded crochet lace is attached on the two falling ends, which adds on to the subtle detailing.</p>",
        "style": "body",
        "align": "start",
        "measure": "normal",
        "layout": {
          "width": "text",
          "space": "s",
          "show": "all",
          "motion": "none"
